# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Environments and secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
# ...except the template, which documents variable NAMES and holds no value.
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json
secrets.*
.venv/
venv/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Qdrant local storage — the collection is rebuilt from data/embeddings/ by
# `python vectordb/ingest.py`, so no database file belongs in git.
.qdrant_local/
qdrant_storage/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Other people's projects that happen to live inside this directory.
#
# These are NOT part of this project and are NOT required to run or reproduce
# anything in it. They are excluded from version control so that this
# repository publishes only its own work.
#
#   aaa-clinical-ragnour/   - the separate reference implementation audited in
#                             eval/project_b_comparison.json and
#                             docs/PROJECT_B_LESSONS.md ("Project B"). Read-only
#                             evidence; never modified, never imported.
#   aaa-clinical-raggehad/  - a separate person's variant of the project. Its
#                             pipeline files differ from this one's; it is not a
#                             duplicate and was deliberately left untouched.
#
#   for ground truth code/     - a third-party "mini-rag" reference service (FastAPI +
#                             Celery + Qdrant/pgvector) kept on disk purely as a
#                             read-only design reference for chunking, embedding,
#                             retrieval and evaluation logic. Not a dependency: no
#                             module in this repo imports it, and nothing in it runs
#                             as part of this pipeline. Its libraries and APIs are
#                             older than ours; only its design decisions are reused.
#
# All remain on disk. The audit conclusions about Project B stand on their own:
# every figure quoted is recorded in eval/project_b_comparison.json.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
aaa-clinical-ragnour/
aaa-clinical-raggehad/
for ground truth code/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/

# Self-hosted fonts and favicon are committed on purpose (see static/), so the
# demo has no external font dependency. Nothing else in static/ is generated.

# Streamlit secrets — never commit. The `secrets.*` rule above already catches
# the real file; the template holds variable NAMES only and is committed on
# purpose, exactly as .env.example is.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
!.streamlit/secrets.toml.example
